    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/flushable-containers",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "flushable-containers"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A flushable container is a named store that accumulates by design — a trash you can recover from, a review preview, a console log. It declares a buffer limit, badges when over it, and offers three flush actions: flush all, trim to limit, and select to prune. What \"flush\" means, and which end of the order is expendable, are declared per container and differ."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "flushable-containers",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/kg-core/flushable-containers.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/gate-tree-mutation",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "gate-tree-mutation"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Reading `bun run gates`' \"NOT clean\" verdict. Why every gate can pass and the run still exit 1, the two causes and how to tell them apart in one command, and the question that settles whether a churning field is a defect in the writer: does it describe the SUBJECT or the RUN?"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "gate-tree-mutation",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/generalise-the-fix",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "generalise-the-fix"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "You have a fix. Before it ships, ask what CLASS of defect it belongs to and whether the fix sits at the right layer — then attack your own answer: name what the fix now catches that the bug did not. Two axes go wrong, SCOPE and STATE, and widening either past the problem is how a fix becomes the next defect. Applies to a bug fix, a schema change, a detector, or a claim in a paper. Use after the fix works and before the pull request."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "generalise-the-fix",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/getting-started",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "getting-started"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Triage what a person means when they ask to create a folio, and route them. Five requests share one sentence — a folio in a new repo, folio-assistant overlaid on an existing repo, a second folio in an instance that already has one, a content object they called a folio, or something the filesystem cannot tell apart. Reads the repository facts, runs them through the folio-intent decision table, asks a selectable question for what facts cannot settle, scaffolds, and reports the published URL. Use whenever a user asks to create, start, set up, or initialise a folio, a paper, a DAK, an IG, or \"folio-assistant\" itself."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "getting-started",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/conduct-core/getting-started.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/github-state-inspection",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "github-state-inspection"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Answer questions about GitHub-hosted state — is a page published, where does it live, did CI pass, does a branch exist — by reading the ref or the API, never by composing a URL or fetching one. The first check for any deployment or 404 question is `git ls-tree` of the publish ref."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "github-state-inspection",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/glossary-build",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "glossary-build"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "glossary-build",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/library/library-core/glossary-build.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/glossary-terms",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "glossary-terms"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Add terms to an instance's glossary: local SKOS terms (folio-glossary/v1) with a definition, a code and links to external SKOS concepts, and references to whole external schemes. Rendered on the glossary/ page; gated by check:glossary. Authored terms go to gettext (.pot) for translation; a paper's glossary is one more scheme."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "glossary-terms",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/library/library-core/glossary-terms.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/goal-review",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "goal-review"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Cold start, then review a time window of activity — sibling sessions, the work plan, issues, change proposals, branches, CI — and prioritise what it finds against goals stated in the owner's words. Inputs are the window, the goals, the scope and the axes; the output is a synopsis (closed, open, needs doing, with effort), a priority queue per goal with selectable next actions, and the instruction gaps met on the way, each recorded as a work item. Use when asked \"what happened\", \"what is stalled\", \"what should we do next for X\", or at the start of a session that inherits parallel work."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "goal-review",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/goal-review.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/graph-detanglement",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "graph-detanglement"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Drive a tangled graph toward a clean partition, so a sub-graph can be split off when it grows too large or when a business reason separates it. The staged practice — declare in place, detangle, isolate, extract — with the seventeen moves that were measured rather than argued, and the failures each one cost."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "graph-detanglement",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/graph-rendering",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "graph-rendering"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Draw any graph in a harness (schemas, processes, a paper's block graph, a Lean proof's dependencies, a detangle partition) so the picture is derived, checkable and readable. Ten rules learned on the UML overview, which engine to lay a graph out with and why, and how each graph kind here applies them."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "graph-rendering",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/graph-management/graph-rendering.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/handover-report",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "handover-report"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Write a handover report: a templated snapshot of an agent's current state, committed as a bean note, so that a session or subagent that stalls, runs out of context, or loses its container can be picked up by another agent without re-deriving anything. Use it when you are told a stall is likely, at the end of every long arc, before a risky or long-running step, and whenever a steward asks for one. Its reader is `stalled-agent-triage`."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "handover-report",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/handover-report.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/harness-requirements",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "harness-requirements"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "What an instance OWES for every directory it declares — a visualiser, a documentation entry, a governing skill, json/jsonld/schema.json serialisations at the directory's URL and at every node beneath it, and a starting README of its own. Read before declaring a directory, before adding a graph kind, and when reading `check:subgraph-coverage`. Carries which obligations are ranked as unmet promises rather than unanswered questions, why the discriminator is \"is this the static knowledge graph\", and which single obligation a harness may never waive."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "harness-requirements",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/harness-tiles",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "harness-tiles"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A tile is a function of the harness watching a directory, not of nodes. Where the tile set comes from, what a tile opens, and the two gaps it reports rather than hides."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "harness-tiles",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/ui/ui-core/harness-tiles.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/html-rendering-qc",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "html-rendering-qc"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "html-rendering-qc",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/ui/ui-core/html-rendering-qc.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/idle-backlog",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "idle-backlog"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "While idle or waiting on a long-running async task (a build, a long compute script, a CI run, a background agent), pull the applicable backlog in priority order and work non-conflicting items instead of stalling. Generalises AGENTS.md's 5-minute idle trigger into a reusable skill. Use whenever blocked on an async wait with no substantive output to produce."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "idle-backlog",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/idle-backlog.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/incremental-render",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "incremental-render"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Rendering only what changed — seeding a build from a previous render, the two edges that decide what must re-run, why a step declares GRAPH KINDS rather than paths, and the rule that could-not-determine always re-renders rather than serving a stale page."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "incremental-render",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/ui/ui-core/incremental-render.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/injection-boundaries",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "injection-boundaries"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Where a value becomes program rather than data — workflow expressions, shell strings, and archive members. What the gate covers, why a step output carries a severity rather than having one, and the argv rule."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "injection-boundaries",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/security/injection-boundaries.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/instance-kinds",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "instance-kinds"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "How to make a new KIND of harness instance — choosing the prefix family, the keep-the-kind's-name default and the owner's right to decline it, which inherited files the new owner may repoint, and what a new GRAPH kind must declare. Read before naming a new instance, before adding a value to the graph-kind registry, and before building a visualiser. Carries the test that usually says \"this is not a new kind\"."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "instance-kinds",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/kg-core/instance-kinds.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/instance-publication",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "instance-publication"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Every asset carries an id and a version and sits in DRAFT. Publication is a state, not a boolean, and `published` is refused by the schema because the formal process does not exist yet. Carries the id namespace rule, why a mirror never takes its subject's identity, and what a consumer may assume of a draft."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "instance-publication",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/integration-audit",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "integration-audit"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Sidecar-invalidation utility for the integration-watcher pipeline. Adds mechanical QA fields (script-reviewer entries) to per-block `.qa.json` sidecars and marks the existing entries stale so the next `qa-sweep` re-evaluates them. Use when a checker bug is fixed in a QA checker module (downstream \"fresh\" entries are now incorrect) or when a registry update adds a criterion the block hasn't been audited under."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "integration-audit",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/authoring/authoring-core/integration-audit.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/integration-backlog",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "integration-backlog"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Dispatcher for the `/integration-backlog <axes>` slash command. Works the backlog identified by the integration watchers (proof, canonical, compute, detangler, one-voice, …) by clustering the open findings into review-sized batches (≤ 49 files per PR — the reviewer-bot limit), proposing each batch to the author via structured AskUserQuestion calls, running `/prepare-merge` on each, resolving review comments (auto if mechanical, structured AskUserQuestion if architectural), then merging — and repeating until the axis is exhausted or the author signals stop. Sister command to `/integration-watch`: the watcher MONITORS for new events; this skill WORKS the backlog the watcher already catalogued."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "integration-backlog",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/integration-backlog.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/integration-watch",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "integration-watch"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Dispatcher for the `/integration-watch` slash command. Routes to one or more of the concrete integration watchers / audits (proof, canonical, compute, detangler, one-voice, consolidation, bibliography, devils-advocate, …). With no argument, lists the available watchers and asks the user which to invoke. With arguments, dispatches the named watchers in parallel (each gets its own Monitor, queue, ledger, and PR-subscription set)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "integration-watch",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/integration-watch.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/integration-watcher",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "integration-watcher"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Abstract parent skill for domain-specific **integration watchers**. Encodes the shared mechanics — Monitor on `origin/main`, PR subscriptions, per-event QA dispatch, queue + ledger, idle backlog sweep, idle author-ask dispatcher, watch-PRs-you-prepare protocol, voice-pass on PR diff, witness-drift CI recovery, billing-quick-fail flake handling — that every concrete watcher inherits. Children fill nine domain-specific slots; everything else is shared here."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "integration-watcher",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/integration-watcher.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/interaction-modality",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "interaction-modality"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Establish how to talk to the person in front of you before deciding what to say — audio, ordinary chat, selectable options for limited hand function, large-type for low vision, plain language — and hold that choice durably so every later session and sibling agent honours it. Covers the accessibility rules a conversational agent can actually keep, the settings surface in the published site, and how to drive a question set from DMN so the SAME logic serves every modality. Use at first contact with a new user, when a user reports difficulty answering, whenever a question is about to be asked, and before any long free-text prompt."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "interaction-modality",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/issue-working",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "issue-working"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Working a tracked issue — announce the branch when you create it rather than when you finish, and re-check the issue for new AND edited comments while you work. Both rules are about the gap between your view of an issue and everyone else's."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "issue-working",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/issue-working.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/kg-contribution-offer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "kg-contribution-offer"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Ask whether agreed requirements should become knowledge-graph content, and as what — in a form the person can answer by selecting. Use at the end of CRDM sign-off, or whenever a body of agreed work could become a skill, a process, a schema or a bean and nobody has been asked. Offers \"none\" as a first-class answer."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "kg-contribution-offer",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/kg-core/kg-contribution-offer.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/kg-export",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
