          "@value": "liquid-templates"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Authoring a Liquid template in this repository — a README template the `subgraph-readmes` Tool renders with liquidjs, or a Jekyll include on the just-the-docs site. Where templates live (inside a declared directory, reached through its id), what a template may read (only what the Knowledge Graph hands it), the leading comment the generator reads as the file's description, includes, whitespace control, escaping, and regenerate-then-commit with the `--check` gate. Read it before adding or changing any `.liquid` file or anything under `docs/_includes/`."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "liquid-templates",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/ui/ui-core/liquid-templates.md",
