          "@value": "opening-brief"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Brief a bean or a topic BEFORE touching anything: what you are doing and why it is worth doing, what you already know and with what provenance, how you plan to do it and what would falsify the approach. Scales with irreversibility, not line count."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "opening-brief",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/package-release",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "package-release"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Cut a release of a repository's packages: decide the next version, write the release notes, tag, and create the release — for any repository, the platform or a folio. Publishing the built artefact to a registry is a separate, later step that a person starts."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "package-release",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/package-release.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/path-containment",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "path-containment"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Turning a value from outside into a path. The two different questions — a URL path versus a single identifier — why collapsing them is a defect, and the three sinks in this repository that had neither check."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "path-containment",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/security/path-containment.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/pending-show",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "pending-show"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Show the current session's pending work — beans list + ledger intent. Read-only."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "pending-show",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/pending-show.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/pickup",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "pickup"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Pick up / continue work on one or more existing open PRs efficiently. Resolves each PR's REAL branch + title + checklist + reviews + CI in one batched pass, classifies CI as billing-vs-real, then dispatches one worktree sub-agent per PR with a filled-in brief, and applies the safe class of review-nit fixes (eval→ast.literal_eval, dead-code/unused-var removal, etc.). Use when the user says \"pick up PR N\", \"continue 1543/1576/1571\", \"work these PRs\", \"address the review on PR N\", or \"take over PR N\"."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "pickup",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/pickup.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/placement",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "placement"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Establish where a new node belongs BEFORE you create it — which instance, which declared graph, which kind of node, and which of the two \"stub\" conventions applies. Read before adding a skill, role, actor, workflow, decision table, schema, tool or content object, and before writing any literal that names one folio."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "placement",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/platform-gates",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "platform-gates"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "`bun test` passing is not the gates passing. What to run before you push, why the list is derived from the CI workflow rather than written down, and what a `*:check` failure is actually telling you to do."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "platform-gates",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/platform-gates.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/pr-description",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "pr-description"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Write or update a pull request's description so that someone who has never seen the work can follow it: the problem, why it matters, how it was approached, what constrained it, the solution, how to use it, and what is not done. Read before opening a PR, before rewriting its body, and whenever the PR's scope changes."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "pr-description",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/pr-description.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/prepare-for-handover",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "prepare-for-handover"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Prepare for a handover: commit and push everything you hold, then write a handover report that cites the commits. Use it when told a stall, timeout or container loss is coming (\"you may stall in N minutes\"), before a long or risky step, or whenever a steward or the owner says \"prepare for handover\". It is the producing half; `handover-report` is the format and `stalled-agent-triage` is the reader."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "prepare-for-handover",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/prepare-for-handover.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/prepare-merge",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "prepare-merge"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Take a feature branch to a clean, conflict-free, green, pushed state so it can be merged with no surprises: base merged in, generated files regenerated, the folio's content-type gates run, then pushed. It does NOT merge and does NOT push to the default branch. Use for \"prepare-merge\", \"make it mergeable\", \"ship it\"."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "prepare-merge",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/prepare-merge-auto",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "prepare-merge-auto"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Full autonomous prepare-merge → resolve → merge pipeline. Coordinates with sibling PRs, resolves review comments, asks structured questions only when blocked, then merges."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "prepare-merge-auto",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/prepare-merge-auto.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/process-state",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "process-state"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Track where you are inside a running process — which task, in which swimlane, under which role — and recover deliberately when you find yourself outside it. Read before completing a workflow step, and whenever something unexpected interrupts one. Covers what to do about notes and stickies you re-anchored while off-process, which leave no trace in the artefact."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "process-state",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/process/workflow/process-state.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/production-vs-exploratory-discipline",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "production-vs-exploratory-discipline"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Distinguish PRODUCTION (derived-only, no fits) from EXPLORATORY (empirical-fit probes OK as shape-hints) from NUMEROLOGY (post-hoc fits to known constants). The hidden-extra-input / empirical-fit antipattern is a common review-churn source: agents promote empirical fits into production scripts, \"closed\" status, dashboards, and named constants without a derivation. This skill is the bright-line guide for which output goes where, the derivation-menu check, and the escalation path for off-menu coefficients."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "production-vs-exploratory-discipline",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/authoring/authoring-core/production-vs-exploratory-discipline.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/publish-verification",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "publish-verification"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Verify what a publish produced BEFORE it is deployed, and alert the publication manager whenever any step after the publish button fails — the verifier set, how to add a verifier, what is in scope, and how the publication manager triages the one alert."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "publish-verification",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/publish-verification.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/qa-report-signing",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "qa-report-signing"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "qa-report-signing",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/qa-reports",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "qa-reports"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Where a QA result lives now. Derived verdicts go to the orphan `qa-reports` branch, keyed by commit, written by the CI job `qa-publish`. Judgements stay on main in the `attestations` graph. Gates compute and judge against a stored baseline, and a missing one is unknown. Read before you regenerate, commit, resolve, cite or delete anything under `test/results/` or `test/attestations/`."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "qa-reports",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/qa-reports.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/qa-witness",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "qa-witness"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The QA projections written to `test/results/witnesses/` and stored on the `qa-reports` branch — what a `qa-witness/v1` document says, which three families produce one, how to read a verdict and the witness behind it, and why \"could not determine\" is a third state everywhere in them."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "qa-witness",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/qa-witness.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/raci",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "raci"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "RACI over this repository's processes — who is Responsible, Accountable, Consulted and Informed for each activity. Three declared edge kinds over the roles and BPMN activities that already exist, not a new party registry. Use it to work out involvement when a project is initiated, and to sketch its breakdown."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "raci",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/process/raci/raci.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/readability-editing",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "readability-editing"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "readability-editing",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/authoring/authoring-core/readability-editing.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/readme-sections",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "readme-sections"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A folio's README is the author's file; the platform owns only the marked regions it generates. How the sync/audit split works, why the whole-file generator it replaced could not, and the third state both tools must report."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "readme-sections",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/ui/ui-core/readme-sections.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/related-work-coordination",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "related-work-coordination"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Before new work takes shape, find the work it touches. Search beans, issues and open PRs for relevance; categorize and summarize every hit; then ask the user whether and how to coordinate. Judgement decides the categories and the recommendation, and the user decides the coordination. Called by CRDM when a requirement is initiated or updated in chat, and by methodology adoption. Process: processes/sdlc/related-work.bpmn."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "related-work-coordination",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/related-work-coordination.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/release-epic-planning",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "release-epic-planning"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Plan and track releases using bean epics. Covers epic creation, story/task decomposition, release readiness tracking, and the relationship between epics and GitHub milestones. Applies to code releases, paper publications, and project milestones."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "release-epic-planning",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/process/workflow/release-epic-planning.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/release-lifecycle",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "release-lifecycle"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Governs the release lifecycle: semver policy, draft/named releases, changelogs, release gating, and the relationship between feature branches, PRs, beans, and releases. Applies to code releases, paper publications, and project milestones. Complements package-release (which handles the mechanics of cutting a release) with the process and policy layer."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "release-lifecycle",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/process/workflow/release-lifecycle.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/render-kg-to-cdn",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "render-kg-to-cdn"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Render a Knowledge Graph, or a list of its Subgraphs, for publication to a CDN at a publication root URL, and report a status and one message. The same step for a staging preview and for a release — only the root URL and the target differ. Names the target's Tool, never its steps: GitHub Pages (`gh-pages`) is one Tool, and it carries its own subprocess."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "render-kg-to-cdn",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/process/workflow/render-kg-to-cdn.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/render-logging",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "render-logging"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Log every render to the publish branch — what was published, removed, restored or deliberately retained — to an append-only log that lives beside what it describes. Use when adding or removing anything on `gh-pages`, when asking \"what happened to this preview\", or before writing a workflow step that deletes a published artefact."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "render-logging",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/ui/ui-core/render-logging.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/render-order",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "render-order"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "render-order",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/ui/ui-core/render-order.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/rendered-verification",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "rendered-verification"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Confirm a UI change by LOOKING at it in a browser and sending the screenshots to the author, rather than describing it. Use whenever a change touches CSS, a Liquid/HTML template, a generated page, the navbar, a board, a sticky or any rendered surface — before claiming it works, and before asking the author to review it. Covers building the site locally, taking the REAL CI build off `gh-pages` when the question is theme chrome or layout, driving it with Playwright in this environment, measuring computed style rather than reading the stylesheet, hit-testing a control's centre because visible is not usable, asserting the conditions so a check cannot pass over an unstyled page, and the defect classes that are invisible to a green gate set."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "rendered-verification",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/rendered-verification.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/repo-conversion",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "repo-conversion"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Lay folio-assistant over a repository that already exists, without losing or silently moving what is in it. Scans the tree read-only, classifies candidate files into library (external source) and content (authored here) with an explicit third bucket for what it cannot classify, puts the three questions the scan cannot answer to the author as selections, and hands ingestion to one agent or a small swarm. Use when a user wants an existing repo converted to a folio, asks to import what is already there, or asks whether their PDFs/notes/drafts can come along."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "repo-conversion",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/conduct-core/repo-conversion.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/retry-backoff",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "retry-backoff"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Every error gets a falling-off retry rate — each wait doubles, with jitter. Read before writing any call that can fail transiently, and before deciding that a failure is worth retrying at all. Exhausting the retries does not change the verdict."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "retry-backoff",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/conduct-core/retry-backoff.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/review-comments",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "review-comments"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Reviewer comments on a folio's edit-set, from a tagged pull-request comment to a structured todo on the review page. Covers the tag a reviewer types, how the comments are ingested into `folio-review-comment/v1` todos, where the published `review-comments.json` comes from and when it refreshes, how a comment follows a renamed block and survives a removed one, who may change a comment's status, and how to change this process. Use when a reviewer asks how to comment on a block, when the review page shows no comments or a wrong one, when editing the ingestion, or when a folio's staging workflow is set up."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "review-comments",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/authoring/authoring-core/review-comments.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/review-heatmap",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "review-heatmap"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The review page's heat map: a section-by-metric table that tells a reviewer of a large document where to look first. Says what each column MEANS and what it must NOT be read as, where each number comes from, what a column says when a build lacks its data, and how the colour was chosen. Use when a reviewer or author asks \"where do I start\", reads a number off the heat map, or asks why coverage or QA say \"no data\"; and before adding a column."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "review-heatmap",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/authoring/authoring-core/review-heatmap.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/role-model",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "role-model"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Actors, roles and skills — who performs a BPMN task, under which swimlane, with which skills. How a role's skill set is resolved through `inherits` and through a subprocess call chain, how a lane binds to a declared role, and how `kg:audit` finds a dangling skill, lane, role or decision."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "role-model",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/process/process-core/role-model.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/sample-import",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "sample-import"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Testing an import of a SAMPLE of a remote source into a knowledge graph or other structured store: scope it, let materialize-remote gate it, land it in the library (permanent) or the kept, unpublished trashcan (trial), import it, and test the import. The gates are called, never copied."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "sample-import",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/library/large-datasets/sample-import.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/schema-management",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "schema-management"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Manage a schema over its life — add one, change one, read the schema graph and its viewer, and act on what the reader could not determine. The layout rule lives in `directory-conventions`; the entity question lives in `data-modelling`; this is the work in between."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "schema-management",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/scientific-accuracy",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "scientific-accuracy"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "scientific-accuracy",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/authoring/authoring-core/scientific-accuracy.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/security",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "security"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The security sub-KG's entry point. What the boundaries are, which machinery already guards each one, and the single rule that unifies them — refuse, never repair. Read this before adding a check, so the answer that already exists is reused rather than rebuilt in a fourth place."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "security",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/security/security.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-skills/serving-renderings",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
